From: kart build <kart@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: spi: mcux_ecspi: abort SDK transfer on completion timeout

If spi_context_wait_for_completion() times out, the SDK transfer handle
was left in the busy state, so every subsequent transfer on the bus (for
any device) failed immediately with kStatus_ECSPI_Busy -> -EIO. A single
timeout permanently killed the whole bus until reboot (observed on
i.MX8MM: one failed ADS8688 transfer bricked the MCP2515 CAN gateway
sharing ECSPI2).

Abort the SDK transfer and deassert the chip select on timeout so the
bus recovers and the caller can retry.

Upstream-Status: Pending [clear upstream candidate]
---
diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi_mcux_ecspi.c b/drivers/spi/spi_mcux_ecspi.c
index 8138e7fdc2a..79812d87fc9 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi_mcux_ecspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi_mcux_ecspi.c
@@ -243,6 +250,16 @@ static int transceive(const struct device *dev,
 
 	spi_mcux_transfer_next_packet(dev);
 	ret = spi_context_wait_for_completion(&data->ctx);
+	if (ret != 0) {
+		/* kart: on timeout the SDK handle would stay busy forever,
+		 * failing every subsequent transfer on this bus (any device)
+		 * with -EIO. Abort the transfer and deassert CS so the bus
+		 * recovers and the caller can retry. */
+		const struct spi_mcux_config *config = dev->config;
+
+		ECSPI_MasterTransferAbort(config->base, &data->handle);
+		spi_context_cs_control(&data->ctx, false);
+	}
 
 out:
 	spi_context_release(&data->ctx, ret);
